From c28c616bbe42cbe892ab6a5c15db03cb16527807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:33:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/70] ppc32: CallCFunction restores the stack pointer with
 lwz on 32-bit

14.6's CallCFunction reloads sp from the back chain with a raw `ld` when
the activation frame is aligned beyond the pointer size (Darwin: 16
bytes), deliberately bypassing LoadU64 so that no POWER10 prefixed load
can insert a nop ahead of the kMaxSizeOfMoveAfterFastCall check.  `ld` is
declared under V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 only, so the 32-bit build does not
compile: use lwz there (one instruction either way, the size check holds).
Found by node/sweep64.py as the only new GATED-mnemonic hit against the
13.6 tree.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
index 34f5e7a..e8b23bf 100644
--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -2743,7 +2743,11 @@ int MacroAssembler::CallCFunction(Register function, int num_reg_arguments,
     int stack_space = kNumRequiredStackFrameSlots + stack_passed_arguments;
     if (ActivationFrameAlignment() > kSystemPointerSize) {
       // Using prefixed load may emit `nop` which then fails the check below.
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
       ld(sp, MemOperand(sp, stack_space * kSystemPointerSize));
+#else
+      lwz(sp, MemOperand(sp, stack_space * kSystemPointerSize));
+#endif
     } else {
       AddS64(sp, sp, Operand(stack_space * kSystemPointerSize), r0);
     }
